<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I066d69cc0f600668b6304b3448bbe5efd9175279" commit="cdb97e77ad7f632cd624a224f5d77100386973aa" commit_message="UPSTREAM: serial: 8250_early: do not save and restore IER in write callback  The IER has already been masked in early_serial8250_setup(), there is no reason to save and restore it every time early_serial8250_write() is called.  Signed-off-by: Masahiro Yamada &lt;yamada.masahiro@socionext.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Peter Hurley &lt;peter@hurleysoftware.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 2cda227bba7e8398c6f8a7792c7f35818187dcc6)  BUG=b:63794014 TEST=check with earlycon and keep_bootcon in cmdline  Change-Id: I066d69cc0f600668b6304b3448bbe5efd9175279 Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/582056 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="582056" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/56/582056/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Icb2e58a03278028d2bb04eca2243ad513a8028fa" commit="98aa0888861543e31a76b8aeb0ec089d81a75410" commit_message="UPSTREAM: serial: 8250_early: confirm empty transmitter after sending characters  The current code waits until the transmitter becomes empty, before sending each character, and after finishing the whole string. This seems a bit redundant.  It can be more efficient by checking the transmitter only after sending each character.  This should be safe because the transmitter is already empty at the first entry of serial_putc().  Signed-off-by: Masahiro Yamada &lt;yamada.masahiro@socionext.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Peter Hurley &lt;peter@hurleysoftware.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit f2bfdb0628d50339a70de475eb2be1c4c1eb9014)  BUG=b:63794014 TEST=check with earlycon and keep_bootcon in cmdline  Change-Id: Icb2e58a03278028d2bb04eca2243ad513a8028fa Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/582057 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="582057" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/57/582057/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Ib1d32c815e4090720173bc71cdefff4937439641" commit="0dcc7c8a49ba86c6f7aaa14b6e4015ef23674377" commit_message="UPSTREAM: serial: 8250_early: squash wait_for_xmitr() into serial_putc()  Now, wait_for_xmitr() is only called from serial_putc(), and both are short enough.  They can be merged into a single function.  Signed-off-by: Masahiro Yamada &lt;yamada.masahiro@socionext.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Peter Hurley &lt;peter@hurleysoftware.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman &lt;gregkh@linuxfoundation.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 004e2ed5cc6d89201140ca96693bf9c0b2945f43)  BUG=b:63794014 TEST=check with earlycon and keep_bootcon in cmdline  Change-Id: Ib1d32c815e4090720173bc71cdefff4937439641 Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/582058 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="582058" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/58/582058/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I38e692df949198c8e8085cb1db52b35584464852" commit="ea6b6fd178d0c075bfdd3198eb3e9e5f6930f7a6" commit_message="FROMLIST: serial: 8250_early: Remove __init marking from early write  The earlycon would be alive outside the init code in these cases: 1/ we have keep_bootcon in cmdline. 2/ we don't have a real console to switch to.  So remove the __init marking to avoid invalid memory access.  Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Tested-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/9846961/)  BUG=b:63794014 TEST=check with earlycon and keep_bootcon in cmdline  Change-Id: I38e692df949198c8e8085cb1db52b35584464852 Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/582059 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="582059" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/59/582059/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I9e9216230329483fd0bfcb44ce23cd15bae864b3" commit="654e726dc80a01dc62b72c64be6e4a8e1152030b" commit_message="sweetberry: allow larger sense resistors  Currently sweetberry hits an integer truncation issue at 2.4 ohm when uA per div goes below 1. We can use 100ths of a uA as the current per div scale.  BRANCH=None BUG=chromium:608039 TEST=log from sweetberry with 10 ohm config.  Signed-off-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt;  Change-Id: I9e9216230329483fd0bfcb44ce23cd15bae864b3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/577051 Commit-Ready: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; " fa